    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Implement a sliding window technique to reduce the complexity of the KNN algorithm to O(SN^2).\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Replace the nested loops with a sliding window approach.\",\n    \"Optimize the loop to reduce the number of iterations.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"--- BEGIN FILE src/solution.cpp ---\\n#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n,s;\\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)\\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \\n            scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n    assert(s<n);\\n    assert(n<8000);\\n    assert(s>0);\\n    assert(n>0);\\n\\n    int sum = 0;\\n    for(int i=0;i<s;i++)\\n        for(int j=0;j<s;j++)\\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\n    int mxSum = sum;\\n\\n    int dir = 1;\\n    int i = 0;\\n    int j = 0;\\n    while(i+s <= n) {\\n        if( (j+s == n && dir==1) || (j==0 && dir==-1) ) { \\n            int exitingRow = i;\\n            int enteringRow = exitingRow+s;\\n            if(enteringRow >=n) break;\\n\\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum -= matrix[exitingRow][k+j]; } \\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum += matrix[enteringRow][k+j]; } \\n\\n            i++;\\n            dir*=-1;\\n        } else {\\n            int exitingCol,enteringCol;\\n            if(dir==1) {\\n                exitingCol = j;\\n                enteringCol = exitingCol + s;\\n            } else {\\n                enteringCol = j-1;\\n                exitingCol = enteringCol + s;\\n            }\\n\\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum -= matrix[k+i][exitingCol]; } \\n            for(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum += matrix[k+i][enteringCol]; } \\n            j+=dir;\\n        }\\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\\n    }\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\n\\\",mxSum);\\n}\\n--- END FILE src/solution.cpp ---\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The sliding window technique reduces the number of iterations by only considering the relevant part of the matrix at each step. This approach significantly improves the efficiency of the KNN algorithm, especially for large matrices.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [\n      \"What is the sliding window technique and how does it work?\",\n      \"What is the time complexity of the sliding window technique?\",\n      \"What is the space complexity of the sliding window technique?\",\n      \"What is the advantage of using the sliding window technique over the nested loops?\"\n    ],\n    \"urls\": [\n      \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sliding_window_algorithm\",\n      \"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/sliding-window-algorithm/\",\n      \"https://www.cs.princeton.edu/~chazelle/teaching/2011/spring/notes/07-sliding-window.pdf\",\n      \"https://www.cs.princeton.edu/~chazelle/teaching/2011/spring/notes/07-sliding-window.pdf\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"
